    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0447" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/239: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-08T10:00:00+08:00">May 8, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 8—1:42 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>312. Shanghai’s May 3, noon.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d424-f1"/> Senior Minister has
                    telegraphed to the Senior Consul at Shanghai informing him of the Diplomatic
                    Body’s approval of the resolution passed by the ratepayers to increase the <pb
                        facs="0448" n="350" xml:id="pg350"/> Chinese members of the Municipal
                    Council from 3 to 5.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d424-f2"/> In this connection
                    Minister Johnson at Nanking has telegraphed the Legation as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I approve of resolution. Please inform the Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d424-f1" n="20" xml:id="d424-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d424-f2" n="21" xml:id="d424-f2-content">
                <p>Chinese representation was increased from 3 to 5 councilors in 1930.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
